I stand up and take my jacket.
It is late, and I have to take the bus home.
Eva follows me out to the door.
"Shall we do something next month?" she asks suddenly.
"I intend to go to an art museum," she explains.
"Do you perhaps want to come along?"
I nod enthusiastically and take my bag.
"Yes, I would very much like that," I answer.
I believe that we will definitely have fun.
I also tell her that I love modern art.
"And I feel that we always talk so well together," I add.
Eva smiles broadly and opens the front door for me.
"We will definitely make a plan soon," she promises.
"I will send you a message on Monday," I say.
I give her a hug and step out into the stairwell.
It has truly been a cozy evening.
